Well, here's a little "ah ha!" idea or several:

1) Don't carry all that crud. Turn every large box and chest you find
into a mini-stash, and abandon all the stuff for which you have no
immediate use in a mini-stash at the top of some staircase.

2) Once you've done Sokoban, suddenly your strength is as the strength
of ten. I found a healer of mine suddenly sporting a strength of 18
while still shoving boulders. This works especially well if you take
the
time to shove around some boulders early in the game just to move
your strength up two or three levels _before_ Sokoban. The advantage
of Sokoban is that never before or after are you going to be exercising
again so intensely or for so long in a row, exactly the circumstances
you
need to advance the last few levels in strength, so save those levels
for
the Sokoban run by advancing as many earlier strength levels as
possible
before you get there. Wizards and other low starting strength
characters
can all employ this strategy to good ends.

3) Remember that crystal plate mail you bypassed as much too heavy
to wear? If your strength is up and your packratitus is cured, suddenly
it isn't too heavy at all, and it _doesn't interfere with
spellcasting_. Go
back and swap out your studded leather or whatever for some nice
crystal plate mail and a four step improvement in AC.

